  "why_this_one": "A floor machine, 3.8 x 4.7 m and 3.1 m tall, 6 of them (one on each of floors 1 to 6): a carved housing whose four taa03 pistons pump up and down 0.5-1 m and whose two t20 orbs spin, on a 30-key clip; red light streams through the holes in its taa02 panels and its pistons' faces, and cyan lightning stars (BITMAP_LIGHTNING+1, lightning2, (0.4, 0.8, 1.0)) spin at bones 15, 19 and 21 (game/world/ornaments.cpp). The user: 'pelase double check all fire and nlight emiters', then 'yes' to the machines.",
  "additive": [
    "taa02",
    "taa03",
    "t20"
  ],
  "additive_from": "MoveObject's arm sets BlendMesh 4 on types 19 and 20 (ZzzObject.cpp:4006-4009): t20's cyan orb drawn RENDER_BRIGHT, its U sliding a sheet a second -- and so here, one sheet a second along U (glow). The red holes are below.",
  "echo": {
    "taa02_body": "taa02",
    "taa03_body": "taa03"
  },
  "glow": {
    "taa02": {
      "scrolls_per_second": 1.0,
      "axis": "u",
      "mask_held": true
    },
    "t20": {
      "scrolls_per_second": 1.0,
      "axis": "u"
    }
  },
  "glow_from": "MoveObject's BlendMeshTexCoordU, -(WorldTime % 1000) * 0.001: one sheet a second along U (ZzzObject.cpp:4003-4009). The stream's sheet carries Chrome01 tinted (1, 0.2, 0.1) whole in its colour and the band in its alpha, and the alpha is held while the colour slides (mask_held), so the red streams behind a slot that does not move, as MU's chrome pass does under the painted one. t20, the cyan orb, slides whole, BlendMesh 4 in both passes. taa03's red centre is not the StreamMesh and stands still, as in MU. Built 2026-10-01 (the user: 'i think most of lost tower orb obhecst was amianted. check if we missed some animation on objects'); before it the red held still, this engine sliding a glow only along V.",
  "echo_from": "RenderObject draws types 19 and 20 twice (ZzzObject.cpp:1035-1059): the whole body in Chrome01 at a flat red BodyLight (1, 0.2, 0.1), mesh 2 (taa02) sliding along U, and then as painted, where taa02's two rings and taa03's round centre are transparent and that red shows through. As the walls' slot (Object04): each such sheet drawn opaque with its holes black (_body), and added over it Chrome01 tinted red inside the holes alone (_slot).",
  "sheet_grade_from": "Ours, as the walls' re_05 (Object04): the housing's grey t17, t18 and panel stone graded to the main walls' warm re_04 and their relief at 0.35, so the machine stands in the same masonry rather than going blue under the cold key.",
  "material_note": "t17 and t18 are carved stone scrollwork, flagstone; the panels the same. The holes, the pistons' faces and the orb are light.",
